    <item>
      <title>Cube Shuffle</title>
      <link>https://bluevisual.tv/personal/cube-shuffle/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 22 Mar 2017 13:38:17 -0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://bluevisual.tv/personal/cube-shuffle/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This was one of my first forrays into Houdini and VEX, as the whole concept of open manipulatable data was so exciting (spoiler: it still is). I wanted to sort of &amp;ldquo;atomize&amp;rdquo; an object, and the reassemble it in a different order.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;vimeo-container project-image&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;iframe src=&#34;//player.vimeo.com/video/257441986?title=0&amp;byline=0&amp;portrait=0&amp;color=00ccff&#34; width=&#34;960&#34; height=&#34;540&#34; frameborder=&#34;0&#34; webkitallowfullscreen mozallowfullscreen allowfullscreen&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;project-image&#34; oncontextmenu=&#34;return false;&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;label for=&#34;lightbox-toggle05&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;img src=&#34;https://bluevisual.tv/project-media/cube-shuffle/cube-shuffle-05.jpg&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;input type=&#34;checkbox&#34; name=&#34;lightbox-toggle5&#34; id=&#34;lightbox-toggle05&#34; /&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;lightbox&#34; oncontextmenu=&#34;return false;&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;label for=&#34;lightbox-toggle05&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;img src=&#34;https://bluevisual.tv/project-media/cube-shuffle/cube-shuffle-05.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/label&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;orthographic-pathing&#34;&gt;Orthographic Pathing&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;m always attracted to cubes, so that was the first shape I decided to try it with, and it grew from there. The geometry of cubes led me to want to make paths that only took cardinal axes one at a time. It does this by joining every vertex and its next neighbor by two intermediate points that lie on each axis independently.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
